WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.837
Planning begins with the learner and the work they need to perform.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:08.784
Define the audience, prior knowledge, learning objectives, course length, tone,

00:00:08.784 --> 00:00:10.758
delivery format, and completion requirements.

00:00:10.758 --> 00:00:15.100
A course for new employees may need more context and examples.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:20.232
A refresher for experienced staff may need shorter modules and stronger job aids.

00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:22.995
Production choices should follow those instructional needs.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:25.364
Storyboards, scripts, narration plans, visual briefs,

00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:27.732
and asset lists keep production organized.

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:30.101
A storyboard maps the learning flow.

00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:32.864
A script explains what will be said.

00:00:32.864 --> 00:00:37.601
A visual brief describes the purpose of each graphic or media asset.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:41.943
An asset list tracks what must be created, who owns it,

00:00:41.943 --> 00:00:46.680
what format is needed, and whether it has been reviewed and approved.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.048
Separate instructional content from production assets.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:52.996
The content explains what learners need to know or do.

00:00:52.996 --> 00:00:56.548
The asset pipeline defines the visuals, audio, video, documents,

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:59.312
and exports needed to teach that content.

00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:04.049
This distinction helps teams avoid treating every paragraph as a graphic request

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:07.207
or every graphic as a substitute for explanation.

00:01:07.207 --> 00:01:10.759
Naming conventions and folder structure are practical quality controls.

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:15.101
Use file names that identify module, asset type, version, and status.

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:17.470
Keep source files separate from exports.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.023
Track approved versions and avoid overwriting final assets casually.

00:01:21.023 --> 00:01:26.154
Even a small course can become difficult to revise when images, audio, scripts,

00:01:26.154 --> 00:01:28.918
and exports are scattered or ambiguously named.

00:01:28.918 --> 00:01:32.470
Decide constraints early: screen size, brand style, accessibility expectations,

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.418
caption requirements, file size limits, LMS constraints, and export targets.

00:01:36.418 --> 00:01:37.997
Those decisions reduce rework.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:43.128
If a course will use 16:9 screens, responsive layouts, SCORM tracking, downloadable PDFs,

00:01:43.128 --> 00:01:48.260
and captioned videos, those facts should influence the asset pipeline before production begins.
